  "response": {
    "html": "<h1 data-chunk-id=\"fd77c7f6-db44-4c5b-83de-6cd89b0bba55\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;border-bottom:3px solid #0d47a1;padding-bottom:6px\">Nebula Drift - Game Design Document</h1>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"e30e926e-cd39-48b9-8b88-2a13b92d8699\" style=\"background-color:#e3f2fd;border-left:4px solid #1565c0;padding:8px 10px;font-size:9pt;color:#37474f\">Vantage Nine Studios - internal - the spine. Numbers live in Mechanics; do not duplicate them here except as prose.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"eb7394fc-bdd0-4b71-832c-a6a3f9f4228f\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Overview</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"bebc83fa-178c-407d-9779-ab074e7aa57a\">Nebula Drift is a single-player momentum-platformer set in the wreckage of a\ncollapsed orbital shipyard. The player is a salvager who cannot fight most of\nwhat lives there and must out-move it instead.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"9ad796dd-7c54-4291-b495-cdb37811ed56\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Design pillars</h2>\n<ul data-chunk-id=\"54cbc67b-8bea-4048-ad1a-14295baab889\">\n<li><strong>Momentum is the reward.</strong> Every system either preserves speed or\nexplains clearly why it took it away.</li>\n<li><strong>The wreck remembers.</strong> Sections the player has stripped stay stripped.</li>\n<li><strong>Legibility over spectacle.</strong> If a hazard cannot be read in one frame at\nspeed, it is cut.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"7bd1e443-0e45-423a-8fab-d3a6b4396bc1\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Core loop</h2>\n<ol data-chunk-id=\"56830339-4959-4c82-bb08-4773317c2812\">\n<li>Enter a sector and read its silhouette for salvage.</li>\n<li>Route through it without stopping.</li>\n<li>Strip what you reached; lose what you did not.</li>\n<li>Spend salvage on traversal upgrades, never on combat.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"6d1eed8f-0319-4d63-a07e-613363d95c05\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Traversal</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"d89ecf30-9600-4981-8c99-e67073aec372\">Traversal is the game. The player has a dash, a wall-run and a grapple. The\ngrapple is the only tool that converts height into speed, so it carries the\nlongest cooldown in the game at <strong>8 s</strong>, and every level is paced\naround that number.</p>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"88790e8e-b03c-4d98-b9be-315aeb958378\">Full parameters live in the Mechanics sub-document, section \"Grapple\".</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"de690cfc-2c1c-4c83-8836-5957bed19361\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Combat</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"125854c9-f236-4966-b59e-1d04c0878aed\">Combat exists to make traversal mistakes expensive. The player has one\ndefensive tool - an overheat pulse - and no weapons.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"92e9998a-071f-42e3-bc6b-7931d79fefa2\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Progression</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"198a1a10-641c-4a50-9849-a113f8720e76\">Salvage buys traversal upgrades in a flat, non-branching order. No skill tree:\nthe team has shipped one before and it cost six weeks of tuning for no measured\nretention gain.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"f9d4291f-d81c-46dd-a269-979a78745354\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Art direction</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"919b5f7a-a4e9-4447-9115-4965f234412f\">Readable-industrial. Detail lives in silhouette, not surface. Full rules,\npalette and reference boards live in the Art Bible sub-document.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"5f3d213d-3c39-44c9-999e-92d2b010d5f1\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Narrative</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"d25fdd6a-c26a-465f-a924-d29002ca2100\">Told through the wreck itself and one voice on a dying channel. Beat sheet\nand characters live in the Narrative sub-document.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"bac056d1-4204-4b08-9b5c-6515dd380663\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Linked sub-documents</h2>\n<table data-chunk-id=\"05c3fbbf-2cc7-4510-bd49-35cf3dc82f85\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #37474f;font-family:Inter , Calibri , Arial , sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"><thead><tr>\n<th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Sub-document</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Owns</th>\n<th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Sections in this GDD that depend on it</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Mechanics</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Every tunable number</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Traversal, Combat, Progression</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Narrative</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Acts, beats, characters</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Narrative</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Art Bible</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Palette, silhouette rules, concept art</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Art direction</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"c8f345db-ce61-4733-a9f1-d2f9753caf44\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Open questions</h2>\n<ul data-chunk-id=\"ae8eafe0-ba4b-4d5d-bdd6-275876b2967c\">\n<li>Does the overheat pulse need a resource cost, or is the cooldown enough?</li>\n<li>Can a sector be re-entered after it is stripped, and does that break pillar 2?</li>\n</ul>",
